Z||000009||88 Database Nut||04-26-2000||12:42 PM||||That IS disheartening Cooter!  Just a general comment, but since I am always on the prowl for 88s, I have seen MANY excellent deals around the country.  One guy bought a Silver 88GT with around 100k for less than $1500. All it needed was a new TC solenoid for the automatic tranny.  He got an outstanding deal, but there are so many more all the time.  I hate to say it, but I think that after 12 -16 years, unless a car is being bought by an Enthusiast who will pay for what he/she feels is worth alot, most Fieros wind up being sold for alot less than we owners want to admit to ourselves.  I've seen some 88 GTs on the market for over a year, with the price slowly dropping from $6K to $3K and lower in some cases.  There is an 88 Formula TTop for sale on the yahoo auctions, current price is $2100 and he'll likely get no more than $3000 if that.  The Fiero Market is great right now for buyers but not sellers, except for a few cases. Same as it ever was, I guess, but surely hard to take.  As prices keep falling for most Fieros, I advise buyers to keep checking the dozens of online used car sources, because the deals are out there, just like Cooter found.  Cooter, GO Get That <BR>Beast!  The wife will understand, and regardless of falling prices that is a GREAT deal (as if you didn't know).  Bring your other GT to the swap meet this weekend and I think you'll get your money back!  GOOD LUCK!||||reg||1
